-- Child Development Co-Savings Act 2001 — THE ENCODER'S TESTS.
--
-- Every expected value is worked by hand from ../source/CDCSA2001.txt; the
-- provision is on each group and the arithmetic where it is not obvious.

§ `Tests`

§§ `Helpers`

GIVEN c IS A DATE, edd IS A DATE, still IS A BOOLEAN, citizen IS A BOOLEAN, later IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A Birth
`birth` c edd still citizen later MEANS Birth WITH
    `confinement on` IS c
    `estimated delivery date` IS edd
    `stillborn` IS still
    `a citizen at birth (or would have been, if stillborn)` IS citizen
    `became a citizen on` IS later

GIVEN c IS A DATE
GIVETH A Birth
`a citizen born on` c MEANS `birth` c c FALSE TRUE NOTHING

GIVEN born IS A DATE, applied IS A DATE, cpr IS A BOOLEAN, pr IS A BOOLEAN, pass IS A MAYBE DATE, citizen IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Adoption
`adoption` born applied cpr pr pass citizen MEANS Adoption WITH
    `child born on` IS born
    `application made on` IS applied
    `the child is a citizen or permanent resident when the application is made` IS cpr
    `the child is a permanent resident (not a citizen) then` IS pr
    `dependant's pass issued on` IS pass
    `an applicant (or the joint applicant spouse) is a citizen on the relevant date` IS citizen
    `the applicant is the natural parent` IS FALSE
    `joint application with spouse` IS TRUE

GIVEN born IS A DATE, applied IS A DATE
GIVETH AN Adoption
`a citizen child adopted` born applied MEANS `adoption` born applied TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE

GIVEN d IS A DATE, dead IS A BOOLEAN, adopted IS A BOOLEAN, withdrawn IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Earlier specified event`
`earlier` d dead adopted withdrawn MEANS `Earlier specified event` WITH
    `occurred on` IS d
    `each child is dead or was stillborn` IS dead
    `each child adopted by another person, not jointly with her` IS adopted
    `an adoption application since withdrawn or refused` IS withdrawn

GIVEN s IS A `Work status`, months IS A NUMBER, days IS A NUMBER, gross IS A NUMBER, daily IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Work facts`
`work` s months days gross daily MEANS `Work facts` WITH
    `status` IS s
    `months of service or of carrying on before the event` IS months
    `days employed or self-employed in the 12 months before` IS days
    `the 90-day overseas conditions are met, if any days were outside Singapore` IS TRUE
    `weekly index` IS 5.5
    `gross pay (or lost income) per week of work days` IS gross
    `total income per day in the prescribed period` IS daily

§§ `Goal 1 — the common measures (s 2; First Schedule)`

-- confinement before 1 April 2025, estimated delivery date on or after it
#ASSERT `an April 2025 Scheme child` (`a birth` (`birth` (YMD 2025 3 30) (YMD 2025 4 5) FALSE TRUE NOTHING))
#ASSERT NOT `an April 2025 Scheme child` (`a birth` (`birth` (YMD 2025 3 30) (YMD 2025 3 31) FALSE TRUE NOTHING))
-- "a child born alive": a stillborn child is not a Scheme child
#ASSERT NOT `an April 2025 Scheme child` (`a birth` (`birth` (YMD 2025 5 1) (YMD 2025 5 1) TRUE TRUE NOTHING))
#ASSERT `an April 2025 Scheme child` (`an adoption` (`a citizen child adopted` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2025 4 1)))
#ASSERT `a January 2024 Scheme child` (`a birth` (`a citizen born on` (YMD 2024 1 1)))
#ASSERT NOT `a January 2024 Scheme child` (`a birth` (`a citizen born on` (YMD 2023 12 31)))

-- "eligibility date": a foreign child — the dependant's pass date; none yet — refuses
#ASSERT `the eligibility date of` (`adoption` (YMD 2025 3 1) (YMD 2025 5 1) FALSE FALSE (JUST (YMD 2025 6 1)) TRUE) EQUALS YMD 2025 6 1
#ASSERT `the eligibility date of` (`a citizen child adopted` (YMD 2025 3 1) (YMD 2025 5 1)) EQUALS YMD 2025 5 1
#ASSERT REFUSED `the eligibility date of` (`adoption` (YMD 2025 3 1) (YMD 2025 5 1) FALSE FALSE NOTHING TRUE)

-- s 2(2): a stillbirth is disregarded before 1 November 2021, not after (aa)
#ASSERT `the specified event number on` (YMD 2021 6 1) `, earlier events` (LIST (`earlier` (YMD 2019 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the specified event number on` (YMD 2022 1 1) `, earlier events` (LIST (`earlier` (YMD 2019 1 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the specified event number on` (YMD 2022 1 1) `, earlier events` (LIST (`earlier` (YMD 2019 1 1) FALSE TRUE FALSE), (`earlier` (YMD 2020 1 1) FALSE FALSE TRUE), (`earlier` (YMD 2020 6 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE)) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `a first or second specified event` 2
#ASSERT NOT `a first or second specified event` 3

-- s 2(2A): born 29 February — 1 year old on 28 February of a common year
#ASSERT `the age in years of a person born` (YMD 2020 2 29) `, on` (YMD 2021 2 28) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the age in years of a person born` (YMD 2020 2 29) `, on` (YMD 2021 2 27) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `below 12 months of age, born` (YMD 2024 5 10) `, on` (YMD 2025 5 9)
#ASSERT NOT `below 12 months of age, born` (YMD 2024 5 10) `, on` (YMD 2025 5 10)

-- First Schedule Part 1: 5 days; T/W = 11/2 = 5.5; 7 days capped at 6 (note 3A)
#ASSERT `the weekly index for` (`the same number of work days every week` 5) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `the weekly index for` (`a pattern repeated over a fixed number of weeks` 11 2) EQUALS 5.5
#ASSERT `the weekly index for` (`the same number of work days every week` 7) EQUALS 6
-- T/3 = 16/3; 4 x 16/3 = 21.33, rounded down to 21 (note 5)
#ASSERT `the lower of` 4 `times the weekly index` (`the weekly index for` (`no regular pattern` 16)) `or` 24 EQUALS 21
#ASSERT `the lower of` 4 `times the weekly index` 5.5 `or` 24 EQUALS 22
#ASSERT `the lower of` 4 `times the weekly index` 6 `or` 24 EQUALS 24
#ASSERT `the flexible maternity days for weekly index` 5.5 EQUALS 44

#ASSERT `at most` 10000 `per block and` 20000 `in all, for` 2 `blocks paid at` 12000 EQUALS 20000
#ASSERT `at most` 10000 `per block and` 20000 `in all, for` 2 `blocks paid at` 6000 EQUALS 12000

§§ `Goal 2 — the co-savings scheme (Part 2)`

#ASSERT `the Government's matching contribution, eligible:` TRUE `, parent contributes` 3000 `, cap remaining` (JUST 2000) EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `the Government's matching contribution, eligible:` TRUE `, parent contributes` 1500 `, cap remaining` (JUST 2000) EQUALS 1500
#ASSERT `the Government's matching contribution, eligible:` FALSE `, parent contributes` 1500 `, cap remaining` NOTHING EQUALS 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `the Government's matching contribution, eligible:` TRUE `, parent contributes` 1500 `, cap remaining` NOTHING

`no incapacity substitutes` MEANS `Incapacity substitutes` OF FALSE, FALSE
#ASSERT `the substitute trustee for` `(f) the trustee lacks capacity` `, the member has a legal guardian:` FALSE `, incapacity substitutes` (`Incapacity substitutes` OF TRUE, TRUE) `, a nominee approved by the Minister:` FALSE EQUALS "the donee of the lasting power of attorney"
#ASSERT `the substitute trustee for` `(f) the trustee lacks capacity` `, the member has a legal guardian:` FALSE `, incapacity substitutes` `no incapacity substitutes` `, a nominee approved by the Minister:` FALSE EQUALS "a person nominated by the Minister"
-- (da): a legal guardian displaces (e)-(g)
#ASSERT `the substitute trustee for` `(e) the trustee dead` `, the member has a legal guardian:` TRUE `, incapacity substitutes` `no incapacity substitutes` `, a nominee approved by the Minister:` FALSE EQUALS "the member's legal guardian (s 4(1)(da))"
#ASSERT `the substitute trustee for` `(e) the trustee dead` `, the member has a legal guardian:` FALSE `, incapacity substitutes` `no incapacity substitutes` `, a nominee approved by the Minister:` FALSE EQUALS "the trustee's personal representative"
#ASSERT `the substitute trustee for` `(g) the trustee unable or unwilling for another reason` `, the member has a legal guardian:` FALSE `, incapacity substitutes` `no incapacity substitutes` `, a nominee approved by the Minister:` FALSE EQUALS "a person appointed by a Director, until a nominee is approved"
#ASSERT `the substitute trustee for` `(a) custody, care and control granted to the parent who is not the trustee` `, the member has a legal guardian:` TRUE `, incapacity substitutes` `no incapacity substitutes` `, a nominee approved by the Minister:` FALSE EQUALS "the parent granted custody, care and control"

#ASSERT `the law the Public Trustee disposes of a deceased member's moneys under, a Muslim:` TRUE EQUALS "section 112 of the Administration of Muslim Law Act 1966"
#ASSERT `the law the Public Trustee disposes of a deceased member's moneys under, a Muslim:` FALSE EQUALS "the Intestate Succession Act 1967"
-- s 8(1): (d)-(f), (g) for a person in default on a false statement, (h) only if not recovered
#ASSERT count (`the means of recovery open to the Government, ground` `(a) made in reliance on a false or misleading statement, document or information` `, a person in default:` TRUE `, already recovered under (d)-(g):` FALSE) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT count (`the means of recovery open to the Government, ground` `(c) utilised for purposes not authorised by the Scheme` `, a person in default:` TRUE `, already recovered under (d)-(g):` TRUE) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT count (`the means of recovery open to the Government, ground` `none` `, a person in default:` TRUE `, already recovered under (d)-(g):` FALSE) EQUALS 0

